{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794446590,"nonce":"3RFyOn0EHEAA1gR04mtcs+CXtN8=","message":"Committed as 15ea513, not pushed.\n\nRecords and enums, asked for by the user on 2026-11-12 after looking at x-idl, which has both and whose model for them was the reference.\n\nWhat a library writes: `#[hxn::data]` on a `pub struct` of `pub` named fields, or on a `pub enum` whose variants hold nothing. Haxe gets `@:structInit class Options { public var label:String; ... }`, made as `{label: \"x\", enabled: true}`, and `enum abstract Mode(Int) from Int to Int` with the library's numbers.\n\nHow it crosses, and why this way:\n- An enum crosses as an `i32`. The adapter matches each variant by name both ways (`value if value == Mode::Loud as i32`, `Mode::Loud =\u003e Mode::Loud as i32`), so nothing is transmuted and a number that names no variant is `Fault::Range`.\n- A record, an `Option` of data and a `Vec` of data cross as bytes: parts in order, laid out by the new `hxn_abi::wire` (a `Reader` and a few write functions, no dependency and no export). The adapter has a generated `hxn_read_\u003crecord\u003e` and `hxn_write_\u003crecord\u003e`; the Haxe class has `hxnWrite` and `hxnRead`, and `hxn.Wire` holds the three helpers that are not one `haxe.io` call.\n- Weighed and not done: x-idl's way, a finalized native object a record with accessors, which costs a call a field and a second ownership model; and flattening a record's fields into parameters, which gives a result no way back on HashLink and stops at the first list. Bytes already cross on every runtime, so this needed no new crossing on any of them, and nesting needs nothing of its own.\n- The model keeps what a value crosses as (`Type::Bytes`, `Type::I32`) and notes the data beside it (`Param::data`, `Param::borrowed`, `Method::returns_data`), as it does for a number. The emitters change only where a value is converted.\n\nWhat data is: `bool`, `i32`, `i64`, `f64`, the narrower numbers with a width, `String`, `Vec\u003cu8\u003e`, an enum, a record, and an `Option` or a `Vec` of any of these, nested as deep as written. A function takes it by value or by `\u0026`, a list also as `\u0026[T]`, and returns it by value, plain or in a `Result`. So `Option\u003ci32\u003e`, `Vec\u003cString\u003e` and `Option\u003cMode\u003e` are parameters and results now, which they were not.\n\nChecked in the reader: bytes that run out, a bool that is neither 0 nor 1, a negative length, a count the bytes left cannot back (before anything is allocated for it), text that is not UTF-8, and bytes left over. On the Haxe side a null record, list, text or bytes where one is needed throws before anything is written; hxcpp would otherwise read a field of null.\n\nThe manifest gained `enums` and `records`, written only by a library that has some, and the WebIDL form writes them as `enum` and `dictionary`, with a member that is an `Option` left optional. A script gets the data classes as they are: they are plain Haxe.\n\nFixture: `Mode`, `Point`, `Settings` (one of each kind of field) and `Shapes` in tests/counter/core/src/shapes.rs; `data()` in Generated.hx.\n\nNot built:\n- Data carried by a future, a stream or a signal, or given by an async function, and data to or from a lent function. An async function does take data.\n- An enum whose variants hold values, and a union. x-idl has both.\n- `usize` as a field. A list of sizes as a parameter works and is checked.\n- A default for a field other than leaving an `Option` out.\n\nRun: tests/counter/run.sh gen-hl on Ash (hybrid, jit, interp, three times each) and stock HashLink on the NUC, gen-cpp, gen-cppia, gen-wasm and gen-emcc; the hand-written hl, cpp and emcc modes; tests/cli/run.sh on Ash and hxcpp; tests/examples/run.sh on Ash; `cargo miri test -p hxn-abi`, 31 tests. Not run: Windows and hxcpp on Linux.","files":null}]}